# Test code: inherits the project configuration, except three checks.
# - readability-function-cognitive-complexity: Catch2 assertion macros (CHECK,
#   REQUIRE) expand to branches, so the complexity of a test case is inflated by
#   the framework, not by the test.
# - clang-analyzer-optin.core.EnumCastOutOfRange: reported inside Catch2's own
#   header (catch_result_type.hpp, a bit-flag enum cast) when a test is
#   compiled. It is in third-party code that the header filter cannot hide from
#   the analyzer.
# - bugprone-chained-comparison: Catch2 expands CHECK(a == b) to
#   `Decomposer() <= a == b` on purpose, to capture both operands. The check
#   reports that expansion in Catch2 3.4 (the Ubuntu 24.04 package) but not in
#   the fetched 3.7.1, so the result would depend on which Catch2 is installed.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.core.EnumCastOutOfRange,
  -bugprone-chained-comparison
